quran[4]{c,v,t}:
  6,91,"They did not pay due regard to the Reverence of Allah when (denying prophethood,) they said: ‘Allah did not reveal anything to any human.’ Say: ‘Who revealed the Book that Musa (Moses) brought as a light and a guidance for the people, which you make into (separate) parchments that you display, while you conceal much (of it)? And you were taught (through that) what you had not known before, neither you nor your fathers.’ Say: ‘Allah.’ Then, leave them alone to play around in their impious discourse."
  6,92,"Blessed is this Book (which) We have sent down, confirming what was revealed before it, so that you may warn (the people of) the Mother of Cities (i.e. Mecca) and those around it. Those who believe in the Hereafter believe in it and are watchful of their prayers."
  6,93,"Who could be more unjust than someone who fabricates a lie against Allah or says: ‘It has been revealed to me,’ although nothing was revealed to him, and he who says: ‘I will reveal something equal to what Allah has revealed?’ If only you could see when the wrongdoers are in the agonies of death, and the angels stretch out their hands (to them saying): ‘Give up your souls! Today, you shall be recompensed with the punishment of humiliation for you have been speaking untruth against Allah, and for you have been arrogant towards His revelations.’"
  6,94,"(Then Allah will say:) ‘Now you have come to Us alone, just as We created you the first time, and you have left behind whatever We had bestowed upon you. And We do not see your intercessors with you, whom you claimed that they were (Our) partners in your matters. Surely, all links between you have been cut (today). And what you have been claiming has abandoned you."
